## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end streaming ingestion, lightweight validation, data quality scoring, and practical cost governance in a beginner-friendly setup.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams + Lambda ingestion
- Lightweight JSON validation and 0–100 data quality scoring
- Parquet storage in S3 with region/date partitioning
- DLQ handling for invalid records
- DynamoDB for regional budgets and a guard lambda to pause ingestion
- Lifecycle policies for cost control; CloudWatch observability

## Code Example
```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  for (const r of event.Records) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(r.kinesis.data, 'base64').toString('utf8'));
    const ok = validate(payload);
    if (!ok) {
      await sendToDLQ(payload);
      continue;
    }
    const score = computeQuality(payload);
    await writeParquetToS3(payload, score);
  }
  return { status: 'ok' };
};
```

